# No free functions in component files

Do not declare a file-level `function` in a component, directive, or container file. Put that behaviour on an `@Injectable` service.

Angular still needs a function where an API asks for one (`ValidatorFn`, a chart formatter). The service owns the logic. The class passes a one-line wrapper.

```typescript
// Wrong — validator sitting beside the directive
function completeSku(control: AbstractControl): ValidationErrors | null { /* ... */ }

@Directive()
export class AdminProductsBaseDirective {
  readonly form = new FormGroup({
    sku: new FormControl('', { validators: [completeSku] }),
  });
}

// Right
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class SkuService {
  completeSku(control: AbstractControl): ValidationErrors | null { /* ... */ }
}

@Directive()
export class AdminProductsBaseDirective {
  private readonly skus = inject(SkuService);
  readonly form = new FormGroup({
    sku: new FormControl('', { validators: [(control) => this.skus.completeSku(control)] }),
  });
}
```

Constants and interfaces stay in `src/app/models`, not in the component file. A method on the class is fine when it only coordinates that screen.
